From bb2ee5eb1fcbe4941bbd3d003f37e62df9142cfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Rowland <simon@simonrowland.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:03:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Stop the legacy LP loop when the iteration cap is reached

LP() cleared iterate only when both of these were true: the step had
either converged or hit max_LP_ite, and PC_checked was 2.

    (gamma_norm < 1e-6 || gi >= max_LP_ite) && PC_checked == 2

PC_checked increments only while gamma_norm < 1.0, and only up to 2
(PGE_function.c, the check at the top of the LP loop). A point whose
chemical-potential step stays at or above 1 never increments
PC_checked, so the iteration cap never fires.

The diagnostic arrays PGE_mass_norm, gamma_norm and ite_time are
allocated with it_f*2 elements. it_f and max_LP_ite are both 256, so
the arrays hold 512 doubles. global_ite starts at 0 and is incremented
before those three stores, so the write at global_ite == 512 is one
past the end. Past that the loop keeps going.

The cap is now independent of the pseudocompound re-check:

    gi >= max_LP_ite
        || (gamma_norm < 1e-6 && PC_checked == 2)

A converged point still waits for two PC re-checks. A point that never
drops below gamma_norm = 1 stops at max_LP_ite. The status assignment
inside the block is unchanged.

Not reproduced as a hang on this v1.9.6 tree. 164 ig solver=0 and
sb11/sb21 points (25 C to 3500 C, 0.001 kbar to 800 kbar, including
pyrolite, Fe-rich, equal-oxide and wet bulks) all exited 0. Single
oxide, zero, NaN and cold-wet bulks did too. sb21 at T = 0 K does not
return, but it is still in pure-phase initialisation (NaN gbase) and
has not entered GLOBAL ITERATION, so that hang is not this loop. The
change is kept because the control flow above does not terminate while
gamma_norm stays >= 1.
---
 src/PGE_function.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/PGE_function.c b/src/PGE_function.c
index 8f918b2..2c341c1 100644
--- a/src/PGE_function.c
+++ b/src/PGE_function.c
@@ -1628,7 +1628,13 @@ global_variable LP(		bulk_info 			z_b,
 		gv.ite_time[gv.global_ite] 		 = ((double)t)/CLOCKS_PER_SEC*1000;
 		gi += 1;
 
-		if ((gv.gamma_norm[gv.global_ite-1] < 1e-6 || gi >= gv.max_LP_ite) && gv.PC_checked == 2){
+		/* Stop on (converged AND PC re-checked twice) OR the LP iteration
+		   cap. The previous form required PC_checked == 2 even for the
+		   max_LP_ite clause. PC_checked only increments when
+		   gamma_norm < 1.0, so a point that never drops below that
+		   threshold looped forever and then overflowed the it_f*2
+		   diagnostic arrays (PGE_mass_norm / gamma_norm / ite_time). */
+		if (gi >= gv.max_LP_ite || (gv.gamma_norm[gv.global_ite-1] < 1e-6 && gv.PC_checked == 2)){
 			iterate = 0;
 
 			if (gv.gamma_norm[gv.global_ite-1] < 1e-6){
